{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Logical Database Structures"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about database structures."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. \t  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "allocate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to distribute or share something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The logical structures allocate the space for all data. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "acquainted "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be familiar with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are supposed to be acquainted with the physical database structures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "granularity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the level of detail and specificity something has"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The data blocks have the finest level of granularity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fine grained "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very specific and detailed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They allow a fine-grained control of datafiles in the disk space"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "personalize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to customize something to a particular way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can personalize four different sizes of data blocks according to your needs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "read only "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a file that cannot be modified"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can make the tablespace read-only. This means you cannot change any of the data; this avoids the need for a system recovery. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about Logical Structures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the extra information you found."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a 200-250 words text talking about logical structures and their characteristics using the grammar and vocabulary studied. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about Logical Structures "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the extra information you found"}, {"type": "text", "content": " I write a 200-250 words text talking about logical structures and their characteristics using the grammar and vocabulary studied. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with my partners"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Supposed To in Affirmative and Negative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Be supposed to</strong> is a grammar structure used when we want to say that someone is expected to do something, or something is expected to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Be supposed to</strong> is used when you expect something to happen, or someone to do something. </br></br>  It follows the <strong>present simple</strong> structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + be + supposed to + verb in base form + complement </div> </br></br>  Example</br> You <strong>are supposed to</strong> go travel tonight. (someone expects him to do it) </br></br>  In negative sentences, we use: </br></br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + be not + supposed to + verb + complement</div> </br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">Michelle <strong>is not expected to</strong> come home early.</div> </br> (People expect her to arrive later)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are supposed to be acquainted with the physical database structures."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I guess I'm not supposed to forget any of this, it's all very important."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Understanding Data Files and Tablespaces "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To understand <span class=\"strong\">tablespaces</span>, first,  we need to know that all data are stored logically in <span class=\"strong\">tablespaces</span>. Inside the <span class=\"strong\">tablespace</span>, we have all datafiles which are connected to a corresponding tablespace. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "See the following chart:"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob03img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Engineer</strong>: You are supposed to be acquainted with the physical database structures; it is time to review the logical database structures. </br><strong>Assistant</strong>: The physical structures refer to the type of files and they are viewable at the operating system level, right? </br><strong>Engineer</strong>: Exactly! The logical structures, on the other hand, are very important because they allocate the space for all data; they allow a fine-grained control of datafiles in the disk space.  They are supposed to help you organize all the files so you can access them easily. </br>"}, {"time": "33700", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Assistant</strong>: The data blocks, as the smallest of the logical structures, have the finest level of granularity, don't they? </br>\n<strong>Engineer</strong>: That's right. All files are stored in them. A data block corresponds to a specific number of bytes, and you can personalize four different sizes of data blocks according to your needs. Then, we have the extent which is a specific number of data blocks that contain the same type of information. </br>\n<strong>Assistant</strong>: Above the extent,  we have the segment. A segment is a set of extents. </br>"}, {"time": "69500", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Engineer</strong>: Correct! A segment can be temporary; and if an extent is full, another one is created into the same segment. The segments are very useful to allocate information. The last structure is a tablespace; we saw it with the physical structures. They contain and group related data blocks, extent and segments. They simplify administrative functions. Besides, they can have small or extra-large files. </br><strong>Assistant</strong>: Are tablespaces supposed to be always online? </br><strong>Engineer</strong>: They are usually online, but they can be set offline to avoid the access to a portion of the database, or they can make the tablespace read-only. This means you cannot change any of the data; this avoids the need for a system recovery. </br><strong>Assistant</strong>: I guess I'm not supposed to forget any of this, it's all very important."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of logical database structures.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list names of logical database structures.   "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about characteristics of different logical database structures."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you to organize information in your laptop? Do you have any logical pattern?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important that companies have and manage their own databases?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "As